&lt;p&gt;HDF files are not supported in the current version of the Java FAIR Data Pipeline API.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/run/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/run/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="running-your-code"&gt;Running your code&lt;a class="anchor" href="#running-your-code"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below is a brief explanation how to make use of the Java FAIRDataPipeline library and actually getting your code to run from the &lt;a href="https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/interface/fair_cli_dev/"&gt;FAIR CLI&lt;/a&gt; command line interface. The actual command to run your Java code is given in the &lt;code&gt;script:&lt;/code&gt; line in the &lt;em&gt;config.yaml&lt;/em&gt;. In my case I run the Java code using &lt;code&gt;gradle run --args &amp;quot;${{CONFIG_DIR}}&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;. You&amp;rsquo;ll have to change this if you don&amp;rsquo;t use gradle.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/debug/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/debug/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="debugging--troubleshooting"&gt;Debugging / troubleshooting&lt;a class="anchor" href="#debugging--troubleshooting"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id="logger"&gt;Logger&lt;a class="anchor" href="#logger"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The javaDataPipeline library uses &lt;em&gt;SLF4J&lt;/em&gt; (Simple Logging Facade for Java).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can either use this with the SLF4J simple logger, or it can bind to your own favourite logging framework.
In order to set the default simple logger to more verbose logging:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;add the &lt;code&gt;org.slf4j:slf4j-simple&lt;/code&gt; dependency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;set the log level:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.setProperty(org.slf4j.impl.SimpleLogger.DEFAULT_LOG_LEVEL_KEY, &amp;quot;TRACE&amp;quot;);&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="running-manually"&gt;Running manually&lt;a class="anchor" href="#running-manually"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
